From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:55:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 98/99] Replace the multi-object wait polling loop with a
 blocking wait (AK::IOThread burned a core on Linux/Android)

Alertable waits polled in 1 ms slices and WaitMultiple truncated the remaining time to whole ms, so
each slice degenerated into a sleep(0) spin until the slice ended (100% CPU, matches the cycle-186
finding that the failed-lock branch was not the spin). Waits now register a WaitBlock with every
handle; Signal/Release/Terminate and QueueUserCallback wake it. Handles are locked in address order
so wait-all stays atomic. Unit tests cover wait-any/all, timeouts, auto/manual events, semaphores,
mutants, many waiters, alertable wake and CPU use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
